      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1906-01-27_WidnesExaminer_art0025" n="art0025">
        <head>Miss Taney's</head>
        <p>Miss Taney's</p>
        <p>Testimony</p>
        <p>Grateful thanks from a girl who suffered—happy ending to an illness of long standing.</p>
        <p>Let every woman read this letter from Miss Beatrice Taney. It is the Wry of a girl's suffering—of °Jimmie weakness, of nervousness and misery, which harassed her through chudaoad and girlhood. It tells you how when tired of life and despondent. Miss Taney was brought back' weary to health, strength, good spirits, and naPPlness by Iron-Os Tonic Tablets. Sparrow Hall, Hindringbam, • Walsingham, Norfolk. For years I have suffered intensely. In fact all lirougu my life. At the age of five I had a serious illness, during which time I was for days lying betwSen life and death, but I WM attended by every good doctor, and he managed to pull me through, but it left me weak. All through my schooldays, I was never well. At the age of fourteen I left school. Up to now I had been living with my parents at Lee in Kent, where I was born. Then my parents moved to Norfolk, and I was Obliged to go with them. After we got to Norfolk\ to live I became nervous, lost all strength and appetite, and the least excitement caused me to faint. I gave up all hopes of ever getting better. I tiled several patent medicines, but none would do me any</p>
        <p>good. It happened one day my mother was looking over the •' Daily Mail," and she saw your advertisement of "Iron-Ox route Tablets." Thinking they would do me do, she purchased a box for me, and before I had finished taking the first box all nervousness disappeared my strength came back, also my appetite, and my faint- ing fits left me completely. Now lam as well as any- body could wish for. Iron-Ox Tablets are the only thing that cured me. They are the best, finest and cherpest medicine in existence, also a perfect cure. I cannot find words to express thanks for the great benefit 1 have received from them, and shall advise frieads who suffer to Igive Iron-Ox Tablets a trial. You have leave to use this letter in any way you please, and I hope that others who suffer the same as I have will be cured. • Signed (Miss) BEATRICE E. S. TANEY. The Story of Miss Taney's sufferings will bring as ilcul%wering throb from the heart of every woman who flows the full meaning of the word arimmia. Her Ylffering, her dependency, and her joyous gratitude at ,he release from anmtnic weakness which Iron-Ox Tables have given her will be understood and appre- ciated by every poor sufferer. But, remember, this letter is a message to you. Miss Taney has written it that You and every other woman in the kingdom may know that Iron-Ox Tablets can mnke you strong and well,and give yon back good healtb,strong pure blood,rosy cheeks. good appetite, strength, happiness. Won't you try ? Won't you let Iron-Ox Tablets help you? A Dainty Aluminium Pocket Packet of 50 Tablets for Is. (Our 4s. size contains 250 dablets ; it is more economical because it gives you five times as many tablets as you get for one shilling.) If your chemist has not got them they will be sent post free on receipt af price by the Iron-Ox Remedy Co Ltd 20 Cookspur- street, London, S.W. ASSOCIATION FOOTBALL.</p>
