      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1906-01-27_WidnesExaminer_art0137" n="art0137">
        <head>OPRNINCI. CHAPTIIRS IN</head>
        <p>OPRNINCI. CHAPTIIRS IN</p>
        <p>:</p>
        <p>T. .11A-1,0 " EXA.MINER</p>
        <p>LOCAL NEWS.</p>
        <p>Coming Events. The annual ball in connection with the Warrington Market Tenants' Association wilt be held in the Parr Hall on February Bth. Two balls have been arranged in connection with the Warrington Women's Liberal Association. The first will be held in the Parr flail on February 7th, and the second at the Lion Hotel on February 21st. Further particulars will be found on page 1 of this issue. At the penny popular concert on Saturday evening, ,the artistes will be Miss Plumpton, Miss Mason, Miss C. Atherton, Mr. H. Plimpton Mr. J. A. Barker (Manchester), humourist ; Mr. A. .adin, elocutionist- ' ' Mr. Simpson, solo concertina; Mr. J. Craik, solo ' violin; the Penketh Tannery Band trio and' Miss Johnson, pianoforte soloist. , Notice. , The Warrington " Examiner "is now published on Friday afternoon, price one penny, and is on sale at the various newsagents at about 4 o'clock. Should any difficulty be experienced in getting the paper the proprietors will undertake to deliver a copy at any address in Warrington by 5 o'clock on Friday after- noon without extra charge. Address all communica, tions to" Examiner Office," Bewsey-street Warrington UNDER THE CLOCK for Good Mon.—Advt. , Popular Penny Concert. The penny Saturday night concerts in the Bold- -in/set Wesleyan Schoolroom has not lost in popularity and on Saturday there was again a crowded audience. The programme had been arranged by Mr. Foreman and consisted of songs which were rendered in excellent style by Miss Woodward, Miss L. Plinstou (winner at the recent eisteddfod) and Mr. Thomas, cornet solos by Mr. W. Rutter and pianoforte solos by Master Bretberton. The humorist was Mr. A. Maybury, who caused much laughter with his sketches. Torestry. The quarterly meeting of the Warrington District of the Ancient Order of Foresters was held at the Horns Inn, Farnworth-in-Widnes ":on Saturday. Bro. P. Peacock, district chief ranger, presiding. The deleontes were as follows :—P.D.C.R. W. Hipkiss, District Trustee J. WaIsh,P.D.C.R. G. Maybury,P.D.C. R. W. Bullock, P.D.C.R. J. Chrimes, P,C.R. VT. Smith. E. Clayton, W, iitancroft, L. Pinch, J. Grayson, W. Hollins, P.D.C.R. W. Orrett, and P.D.C.R. T. Hollins. After transacting the quarterly business the District Secretary Bro. L. Davies read the valuation - -- . E. J. Farnworth, the valuer of the December 31st, 1904, in which he i district was worth 20s. 2d. in the £. hat the Warrington district should be the holding of a high court, and a tee was appointed to consider what taken towards security, the approval itives of the next High Court meeting It was also agreed that the repro- le North-Western Federation should m before their next meeting with the ig their support and assistance. Tea le Hostess, Mrs. Twigg, A smoking tjoyable character was subsequently</p>
