      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1906-01-27_WidnesExaminer_art0142" n="art0142">
        <head>INFIRMARY BALL.</head>
        <p>THE INFIRMARY BALL.</p>
        <p>BRILLIANT FUNCTION.</p>
        <p>The Infirmary Ball which took phice at the Linn Hotel on Thursday evening was a brilliant and highly successful function: It is indeed gratifying to find that this annual effort on behalf of the funds of a worthy institution still calls forth such a hearty response, for the need for generous help was never greater than at present. The work of the Infirmary increases rapidly each year and a scheme of extension will shortly have to be undertaken • „</p>
        <p>The arrangements for the ball had been admirably carried out by the following ladies committee : President, Mrs. Picktnere, The Mayoress (Mrs. Bolton), Lady Greenall, Mrs. Airey, Mrs. Armitage, Mrs. J. D. Buckton, Mrs. George Dakin, Mrs. John Fairclough, Mrs. Fox, Mrs. Henry Greenall, Miss Litton, Mrs. Long, Miss Massy, Mrs. Monks, Mrs. Mont.°, Mrs. J Charlton Parr, Mrs. H. V. Pigot, Mrs.lW. P. Rylands, Mrs. John White, Mrs. Willis. Mr. W. Peter R,ylands discharged the secretarial duties and his willing ser- vices were largely responsible for the success attained.</p>
        <p>The scene in the ballroom was a strikingly pictur- • esque one. The decorations were lavish and tasteful, having been carried out by Mr. Ralph Johnson. The effect was heightened by the introduction of flowers and plants which had been kindly lent by Lady Greenall, Mrs. J. Chariton Parr, Mrs. Henry Greenall, and Mrs. Long. The ladies who assisted in decorating were Mrs. Parr, Mrs. Henry Greonall, Mrs. Hartley, and Mrs. W. P. Rylands. It was a matter of great regret that owing to indisposition, Mrs. Pickmere, the president of the Ladies Canamittee, was unable to be • present at the ball. . .</p>
        <p>Mr. Vetter's well-known band was in attendance and a programme of twenty-one dances was gone through. The stewards were Lieuten,mt-Colonel J.A. Edelesten, Major It. L. Hartley (Kings' Liverpool Regiment)' Major J. D. Fairclough, Captain G. R. Crosfield, Dr. E. E. Bowden, Mr. John Coxon, Mr. Henry Greenall, Mr. James Hepherd, Mr. Roger C. Parr, and Dr. Reginald Smith. Dancing commenced at nine o'clock and was continued with zest until the early hours of the morning. The catering was in the hands of Mr. John Le, the proprietor of the hotel,and gave complete satisfaction The following is a list of the ladies and gentlemen present :</p>
        <p>Mr. G. G. Ainsworth Mr. R. H. Airey Mr. T. Airey Mrs. Airey . Miss Airey Miss Connie Airey Miss Banning Miss A. Baroneby Miss Bird (York) Mr. H. McDonald Blair Miss B. Blair Miss T. Blair Mr. W. Bleakly Miss Blackly Mr. ,J. W. Boumphrey Dr. and Mrs. Bowden Mr. H. W. Brewtnall ( Didsbury) Captain Bundock Mr. Cbandley Mr. Corbett • Mr. and Mrs. John Coxon Captain G. R. Crosfield Mr. A. V. Dakin , Mr. Thos. Day (Rowton) Mr. T. S. Dumbreck Mr. A. H. Duncan I Mrs. Eckersley Colonel and Mrs. Edelsten Miss Edmonson Major J. D. and Mrs. Fairclough , Mr. Egerton Fairclough Mr. Lionel Fairclough I Miss Faircloug:h Miss Helen Fairclou,gh Mr. and Mrs. Field Dr. and Mrs. Ed. J. Fox Mr. and Mrs. P. F. Frith Mrs. F. Aylmer-Frost Miss E. Gardner Miss Geddes Miss Mary Gornall (Thal- wall) Mr. Arthur Gough Mr. Hugh F. Gough Ur. Cyril P. Gough Mr. and Mrs. H. Greenall Mr. J. Greenall Mr. Greg Mr. Grundy Miss Grundy Miss E. Grnndy Major and Mrs. Hartley Mr. and Mrs. Haslam Mr. and Mrs. JAS. Hepherd Mr. W. N. Hutchings Miss Hutchings Miss Jackson Mr. W. Pier Jones Dr. G. Harold Joseph Mr. Wage Mr. Layton Mr. Alan Lister-Kaye Miss K. Lister-Kaye</p>
        <p>Miss Dorothea Lister- Kaye Miss Mildred Lloyd (Litch- field) Miss Litton Miss 'l:Ti lls</p>
        <p>Mr. and Mrs. F. W. Monks Miss Dorothy Monks Mr. H. R. Monro Mr. and Mrs. H. Percy Mortimer Captain G. P. Mott (S. Lancs. Itegt.) 3lrs. Mott Mr. Geoffrey Owen Mr. H. Owen Miss Rath Owen Mr. and Mrs. Segar Owen Mrs. Parr Mr I' to,,er C. Parr Miss Parr Mr. Pawson .</p>
