        <p>RNITTSFORD PARLIAMBNTARY ELECTION. Rock Bank, Bollington. January 24th, 1906. TO THE ELECTORS.—I wish to take the earliest opportunity of publicly acknowledging the honour which you have conferred upon me in electing me to represent you in Parliament. Whilst my special thanks are due to those who bare worked and recorded their votes for me I hope that now the contest is over party feeling may subside and that I may feel that it is my privilege to represent the con- stituency as a whole. Assuring you of my devotiontourys itofuoribnft:lrley.sts, Yours ALFRED J. RIND.</p>
