        <p>PADGATE. WESLEY Guir.n.—Last Monday evening in the Wesleyan Schoolroom, Padgate, Mr. Cutland gave a paper on "Russian Life at Home." The essayist showed that he had given some attention to his subject and he handled it very well. The essay was much appreciated and Mr. Cutland was thanked for his efforts. WESLEYAN BIBLE CLASS.—Last Sunday afternoon before a good attendance Mr. R. H. Sutton of Warring- ton, introduced man able paper the subject of "Public Worship "in which he" showed that not only did man owe the duty to his Creator, but also to his brother man and also "that it was the highest wisdom for men to assemble themselves together for the purpose of public worship and thus to spiritually strengthen each other. An interesting discussion followed in which Messrs. Brough, England, Hall and Ptinston took part.</p>
